When tagging a new release (e.g. 5.0.0) on github after
suitable testing of the candidate, ensure the Changelog is
updated and commit.

From
https://github.com/jonmacs/jove/actions/workflows/testbuild.yml
choose the latest build, which ought to be all green.

Download the following output files (the number ? after
container or hosted might differ slightly depending on the
order they run in)

In a temporary directory, download:

DIST-container-?-debian_11.zip
DIST-container-?-alpine_3.9.zip
DIST-container-?-centos_7.zip
DIST-hosted-?-ubuntu-24.04-arm.zip

unzip -x -j DIST-container-?-debian_11.zip '*/jove_*.deb' '*/*.tgz' '*/*.zip'
unzip -x -j DIST-container-?-centos_7.zip '*/*.rpm'
unzip -x -j DIST-container-?-alpine_3.9.zip '*/*static.tar.gz'
unzip -x -j DIST-hosted-?-ubuntu-24.04-arm.zip '*/jove_*.deb'

rm DIST-*.zip

Something that looks like the following files should remain:

jove-5.0.0-10.el7.x86_64.rpm
jove-5.0.0-i686-w64-mingw32.zip
jove-5.0.0-x86_64-alpine-linux-musl-static.tar.gz
jove-5.0.0-x86_64-w64-mingw32.zip
jove-5.0.0.tgz
jove500s.zip
jove_5.0.0-1_amd64.deb
jove_5.0.0-1_arm64.deb
jove_5.0.0-1_i386.deb

I run pkg/dos/testdos.sh to generate a MS-DOS
DIST/joveNNNd.zip (copy over to the temporary directory)

Generate a self-extracting form using
	cat pkg/dos/UNZIPSFX.EXE DIST/jove???d.zip > DIST/jove500d.exe
	zip -A DIST/jove500d.exe

After some testing, upload those as assets to the tag.

To test, run a container (podman) of an ubuntu with this dir
exported to it with -v, and try 
	dpkg -i *_amd64.deb
which should install jove, perhaps with a warning, then test jove
then uninstall with
	dpkg -r jove

Repeat for *_i386.deb

Then mkdir /tmp/testjove and unpack *-static.tar.gz in that directory,
and run jove-*-x86_64-alpine-linux-musl-static/jove.
(XXX this needs the musl package installed so it can find the loader,
doesn't this defeat the purpose of a static binary)

I test the mingw tars on a couple of Windows VMs (I have a
WinXP and Win7) and a real Win11 box.

Test the DOS self-extracting version in a new dosbox.

For minimal testing (need to improve this):

I usually ensure that the teachjove command works, that
describe-command works, run a shell command, test an
interactive shell, do a spell-check, unpack jove*.tgz and if
not Windows, run compile-it in that directory using
./jmake.sh as the compiler command, look up a tag, fill a
para, change right and left and try again.  delete a
close-brace and reinsert it to make sure formatting works,
same for a paren.  Hop around screen and file (forward and
back for chars, words, paras, screen, start and end of file;
then with repeats).  Turn on line numbering and hop around.
Turn off and hop around.
